  "privacyBody": "Last updated: November 6, 2026\n\nThis policy covers Pic Merge for Android and iOS and the Pic Merge Chrome extension (the \"App\").\n\nWhat the App does with your files\nThe App reads the images and PDFs you choose and combines them into a single file on your device. Your files are never sent to a server, and the App has no account, advertising or analytics.\n\nWhat is stored, and where\nEverything below stays on your device or in your browser:\n\n- Files you save, in the folder you use: the default folder or one you choose.\n- Recent history: for each save, the time, format, number of items, the result file's name, size and dimensions, the save folder's name, the layout direction, and the result. The mobile app also keeps each item's name, pixel size and file size and the scale applied, and keeps all of this in a local database until the App is deleted. The extension keeps the last 50 saves in browser storage.\n- Your chosen save folder, if you pick one instead of the default.\n- Temporary files made while processing. They are deleted when processing ends, when you remove the item from the list, at your next share, or the next time you start the App.\n\nOriginal images and their paths are not kept in the App. The App does not collect, sell or share any of this data, and the developer cannot access it. Deleting the App removes its stored data, except files you saved to a folder outside the App.\n\nAndroid app backup is turned off for the App. On iOS, your device's own backup, such as iCloud Backup, may include the App's data and the files in its folder, depending on your device settings.\n\nPermissions\n- Android: no internet, storage or camera permission is requested. Files are chosen through system pickers and photos are taken with the system camera app.\n- iOS: the system asks for your permission the first time you use the camera.\n- Chrome extension: no permissions are declared. If you choose a save folder, your browser asks for access to that folder.\n\nSending feedback\nThe mobile app's Send feedback option opens your device's mail app with the address and subject filled in. The subject includes the app version, device model and OS version, and you can edit it. Nothing is sent unless you send it yourself. Your message is then handled by your mail provider, and the developer receives what you send.\n\nOther services\nIf you share a file, your device's share sheet or the app you choose handles it. If you obtained the App from an app store, that store's own privacy terms apply to the store.\n\nChanges\nThis policy may change. Changes are published in this document.\n\nContact\nyncdev@gmail.com",
  "@privacyBody": {
    "description": "Full privacy policy. Translate faithfully: do not add promises or anything that takes on responsibility. Keep the address."
  }
